    "memoText": "\n \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 363\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 7862, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to amend the public authorities law, in relation to allowing\n      two  automatic free transfers for riders using pay-per-ride Metro-\n      cards\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This legislation would require the Metropolitan Transportation Author-\nity (MTA) to provide two automatic free  transfers  for  riders  between\nlocal  bus  and  subway rides, or between local bus rides, provided that\nthe original ticket was purchased no more than two hours prior.\n \n  As I previously noted in last year's veto message to this legislation,\nI requested the MTA take immediate steps to  expand  the  free  transfer\npolicy  to ensure that subway and bus customers who have paid for a trip\nwith a MetroCard can complete their trip for a single fare during  major\ndisruptions in service, whether those changes are planned or unplanned.\n \n  Policies  were thereafter adopted by the MTA in January of 2018, which\ninclude authorizing bus operators to issue up to two paper transfers  in\nresponse  to planned or unplanned service diversions and allowing subway\nstation staff to issue up to two general order transfers during  planned\ngeneral order service disruptions.\n \n  These  policies achieve the intended goal of this legislation. For the\naforementioned reason, I am constrained to veto this legislation.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
